$ npx @atlaskit/ads-cli component AvatarGroup
AvatarGroup
@atlaskit/avatar-group

Props (16)
  appearance                 "grid" | "stack" | undefined
  Indicates the layout of the avatar group. Avatars will either be overlapped in a stack, or laid out in an even grid formation. Defaults to "stack".
  avatar                     AvatarComponent | React.ElementType<AvatarProps, keyof React.JSX.IntrinsicElements> | undefined
  Component used to render each avatar.
  borderColor                string | undefined
  Typically the background color that the avatar is presented on. Accepts any color argument that the CSS border-color property accepts.
  boundariesElement          "viewport" | "window" | "scrollParent" | undefined
  Element the overflow popup should be attached to. Defaults to "viewport".
  data                       (AvatarPropTypes & { name: string; key?: string | number | undefined; })[]
  An array of avatar prop data, that are spread onto each `avatar` component. For further usage information on AvatarPropTypes, the supported props for `avatar`, refer to [Avatar's prop documentation](https://atlassian.design/components/avatar/code).
  isTooltipDisabled          boolean | undefined
  Disables tooltips.
  label                      string | undefined
  Text to be used as aria-label for the list of avatars. Screen reader announcement with default label, which is `avatar group`, is `list, avatar group, X items`. The label should describe the `AvatarGroup`'s entities, for instance: - `label="team members"`, screen reader announcement would be `list team members, X items` - `label="reviewers"` screen reader announcement would be `list reviewers, X items` When there are several AvatarGroups on the page you should use a unique label to let users distinguish different lists.
  maxCount                   number | undefined
  The maximum number of avatars allowed in the list. Defaults to 5 when displayed as a stack, and 11 when displayed as a grid.
  moreIndicatorLabel         string | undefined
  Text to be used as aria-label for the more indicator. If provided, this will be used exactly as-is for the aria-label. If not provided, but an `aria-label` is provided via `showMoreButtonProps`, that will be used instead. If neither is provided, the aria-label will default to "N more people" where N is the number of people that are not visible (e.g. "5 more people").
  onAvatarClick              onAvatarClickHandler | undefined
  Handle the click event on the avatar item. Note that if an onClick prop is provided as part of avatar data, it will take precedence over onAvatarClick.
  onMoreClick                React.MouseEventHandler<Element> | undefined
  Take control of the click event on the more indicator. This will cancel the default dropdown behavior.
  overrides                  AvatarGroupOverrides | undefined
  Custom overrides for the composed components.
  shouldPopupRenderToParent  boolean | undefined
  Determines whether the 'show more' popup has `shouldRenderToParent` applied.
  showMoreButtonProps        Partial<React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLElement>> | undefined
  Provide additional props to the MoreButton. Example use cases: altering tab order by providing tabIndex; adding onClick behaviour without losing the default dropdown
  size                       AvatarGroupSize | undefined
  Defines the size of the avatar. Defaults to "medium". Note: The "xxsmall" (16px), legacy "xsmall", and "UNSAFE_xsmall" (20px) sizes that exist on Avatar are not supported here because elements such as the more indicator cannot be displayed in an accessible manner at those sizes.
  tooltipPosition            "top" | "bottom" | undefined
  Where the tooltip should appear relative to its target. Defaults to tooltip position "bottom".

Examples (1):

Example 1
  tsx                                                                                               
  import AvatarGroup from '@atlaskit/avatar-group/avatar-group';                                    
  const Example = (): React.JSX.Element => (                                                        
    <AvatarGroup                                                                                    
      appearance="stack"                                                                            
      size="large"                                                                                  
      onAvatarClick={console.log}                                                                   
      data={[                                                                                       
        { key: 'uid1', name: 'Bob Smith' },                                                         
        { key: 'uid2', name: 'Design System Team', appearance: 'square' },                          
        { key: 'uid3', name: 'Review Agent', appearance: 'hexagon' },                               
        { key: 'uid4', name: 'Carol Davis' },                                                       
      ]}                                                                                            
      maxCount={3}                                                                                  
    />                                                                                              
  );                                                                                                
  export default Example;                                                                           

